          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Page No. 170"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.123,
            0.293,
            0.144
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Figure it Out"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.153,
            0.847,
            0.192
          ],
          "content": "1. The Earth travels approximately 940 million kilometres around the Sun in a year. How many kilometres will it travel in a week?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.199,
            0.482,
            0.217
          ],
          "content": "**Ans.** We have 52 weeks in a year."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.208,
            0.218,
            0.54,
            0.237
          ],
          "content": "We know that 1 million = 10 lakh"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.209,
            0.238,
            0.567,
            0.257
          ],
          "content": "So 940 million km = 940,000,000 km"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.209,
            0.259,
            0.395,
            0.277
          ],
          "content": "So, 940000000 : 52"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.208,
            0.278,
            0.784,
            0.298
          ],
          "content": "Let x be the number of kilometers it travels in a week then"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.21,
            0.3,
            0.335,
            0.329
          ],
          "content": "\\frac{940000000}{52}=\\frac{x}{1}",
          "image_source": "images/page_25_equation_9.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.205,
            0.331,
            0.36,
            0.349
          ],
          "content": "\\mathrm{or} \\; x = 18076923",
          "image_source": "images/page_25_equation_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.204,
            0.35,
            0.675,
            0.369
          ],
          "content": "Hence the Earth travels 18076923 km in a week."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.379,
            0.618,
            0.528
          ],
          "content": "2. A mason is building a house in the shape shown in the diagram. He needs to construct both the outer walls and the inner wall that separates two rooms. To build a wall of 10-feet, he requires approximately 1450 bricks. How many bricks would he need to build the house? Assume all walls are of the same height and thickness."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.625,
            0.382,
            0.869,
            0.512
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_25_image_13.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.535,
            0.562,
            0.554
          ],
          "content": "**Ans.** Bricks required for 10 ft wall = 1450"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.21,
            0.555,
            0.422,
            0.573
          ],
          "content": "Than ratio is 10:1450"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.21,
            0.574,
            0.846,
            0.613
          ],
          "content": "Now total length of walls = 12 + 12 + 12 + 15 + 9 + 15 + 9 + 9 + 9 + 6 = 108 ft."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.21,
            0.615,
            0.514,
            0.633
          ],
          "content": "Let no. of bricks required be x,"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.21,
            0.635,
            0.433,
            0.653
          ],
          "content": "Now 10 : 1450 :: 108 : x"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.21,
            0.656,
            0.446,
            0.685
          ],
          "content": "Or, x = <u>1450 × 108</u> 15660 10"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.21,
            0.687,
            0.584,
            0.706
          ],
          "content": "Number of bricks required are 15660."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.717,
            0.287,
            0.737
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Page No. 175"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.75,
            0.293,
            0.773
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Figure it Out"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.782,
            0.637,
            0.802
          ],
          "content": "1. Divide ₹4,500 into two parts in the ratio 2 : 3."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.808,
            0.524,
            0.828
          ],
          "content": "**Ans.** Two parts are ₹ 1800 and ₹ 2700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.838,
            0.847,
            0.894
          ],
          "content": "2. In a science lab, acid and water are mixed in the ratio of 1 : 5 to make a solution. In a bottle that has 240 mL of the solution, how much acid and water does the solution contain?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.901,
            0.658,
            0.921
          ],
          "content": "**Ans.** In solution, acid is 40 mL and water is 200 mL."
        },
        {
